# Sanity — the CMS powering this site's content (projects, process, skills,
# about, contact, and job-application variants). Without these set, every
# page falls back to the local seed data in src/lib/data/ automatically —
# the site works either way, this just switches it to live content.
#
# Get these from sanity.io/manage after creating a project (see README.md
# "CMS setup" for the full walkthrough). Copy this file to .env.local and
# fill in the values — .env.local is gitignored, never commit real values.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_API_VERSION=2025-01-01

# --- Only needed once, when migrating content from the OLD portfolio's
# Sanity project. Not read by the app itself — see scripts/sanity/README.md.
# OLD_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# OLD_SANITY_DATASET=production
# OLD_SANITY_TOKEN=
# NEW_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
# NEW_SANITY_DATASET=production
# NEW_SANITY_TOKEN=
